{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ManifoldVolumeBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ManifoldVolumeBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.vol_eq_sum_of_realises","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.vol_eq_sum_of_realises","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumeBridge.lean#L219-L223","doc":"The volume of a realised element, written out as the sum of Bloch–Wigner values of\nthe shapes. Composes the bridge with `volume_def`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.vol_eq_rotateAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.vol_eq_rotateAt","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumeBridge.lean#L208-L217","doc":"**The bridge is compatible with the arc's proved relabelling invariance.**\n\nComposes the hypothesis with the unconditional `volume_rotateAt` of §1: if `T` realises\n`m`, then the relabelled triangulation computes the same number. A consistency check on\nthe hypothesis rather than a consequence of the geometry — but it is derived, and it\nwould fail if the two halves disagreed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.vol_eq_of_two_realisations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.vol_eq_of_two_realisations","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumeBridge.lean#L197-L206","doc":"**Any two realising triangulations have the same volume.**\n\nDerived, not projected: the bridge is applied to each triangulation and the two\nequations are composed. This is the statement that would make \"the volume of the\nmanifold\" well defined, and it is the first thing one would want from the bridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.realisable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.realisable","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumeBridge.lean#L191-L191","doc":"**Non-triviality, and it is load-bearing.**  Without it the class admits the\ndegenerate model `Realises := fun _ _ => False`, under which `vol_eq_of_realises`\nholds vacuously and the class asserts nothing about geometry -- the same failure the\ncorpus records for the birthday axioms, where a two-valued function satisfies all six.\nThat model was CONSTRUCTED and typechecked before this field was added; with the field\nit no longer elaborates.  A carrier must assert something (AGENTS.md §3b-tax). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.vol_eq_of_realises","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.vol_eq_of_realises","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumeBridge.lean#L183-L183","doc":"**The bridge.** A realising triangulation computes the volume. This is the\nhypothesis; the theorems below compose it rather than restate it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.Realises","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.Realises","kind":"def","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumeBridge.lean#L180-L180","doc":"`Realises T m` : the ideal triangulation `T` realises the structure on `m`.\nThurston's hyperbolisation is what would produce inhabitants of this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.vol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.vol","kind":"def","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumeBridge.lean#L177-L177","doc":"The volume of an element of `M`. Undefined in this corpus; supplied by the\nhypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge.mk","kind":"ctor","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumeBridge.lean#L174-L174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HyperbolicVolumeBridge","kind":"class","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumeBridge.lean#L169-L191","doc":"The triangulation-to-manifold volume bridge, carried as an explicit hypothesis.\n\n**No instance is provided, and providing one would be a defect** unless it came with an\nactual theory of hyperbolic 3-manifolds. The point of the class is to make every\ndownstream statement wear its dependence in its type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.volume_rotateAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.volume_rotateAt","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumeBridge.lean#L144-L156","doc":"**Relabelling one tetrahedron does not change the triangulation's volume.**\n\nThe sum differs in exactly one summand, and that summand is unchanged by\n`IdealTetrahedron.volume_rotate`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.rotateAt_tet_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.rotateAt_tet_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumeBridge.lean#L140-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.rotateAt_tet_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.rotateAt_tet_self","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumeBridge.lean#L136-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.rotateAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.rotateAt","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumeBridge.lean#L131-L134","doc":"Relabel the `i`-th tetrahedron of a triangulation, leaving the others alone. ","signatureChunk":0}]}